      "heading_context": "## Old World → New World Bridges",
      "headers": [
        "You know it as…",
        "It relates to MST via…"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Spanning Tree Protocol (STP, 802.1D)",
          "builds *a* spanning tree to kill L2 loops — RSTP uses path *cost*, edging toward minimum"
        ],
        [
          "Network/cluster cabling to minimize cost",
          "the textbook MST application (least cable to connect all sites)"
        ],
        [
          "Single-linkage hierarchical clustering",
          "the merge order *is* Kruskal — clusters merge by nearest pair"
        ],
        [
          "Circuit / chip net routing (minimize wire)",
          "Steiner-tree relaxes to MST when no extra junctions allowed"
        ],
        [
          "Image segmentation (Felzenszwalb)",
          "MST-based region merging on the pixel graph"
